# One GPC's IPL, captioned -- ipl-one-gpc.script with the commentary a viewer
# needs.  Same parameters, same waits, same order:
#
#   script ipl-one-gpc-subtitled.script gpc=2 crt=2 idp=2 kb=KB2
#
#   gpc   the GPC column the O6 controls act on, 1-5
#   crt   the CRT its IPL display goes to, and the one waited on
#   idp   the IDP given the spring-loaded LOAD toggle
#   kb    the keyboard ITEM 1 EXEC is typed on: KB1, KB2 or KB3
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE rather than captions in the original: the original is
# played by every unattended run in the tree, where a caption is at best
# wasted work and at worst a window nobody asked for.  A video wants the
# talking; a measurement does not.  The two stay in step because this file is
# the other one with subtitle lines interleaved and NOTHING ELSE changed --
# if you alter one, alter both.
#
# The waits are the point and are kept verbatim.  Read ipl-one-gpc.script's
# own comments for why 'new-screen' has to come before 'title' (three
# computers share CRT2, and a stale GPCIPL MENU satisfied the title test
# instantly) and why the timeouts are sized for the slowest host we own.
# A caption budget must never become a guessed delay: every caption here sits
# between actions that are themselves gated on a wait.

+0   subtitle Let's do the Initial Program Load (IPL) for GPC $gpc.
+3   gpc $gpc
+1   subtitle Point at Mass Memory Unit 1 (MMU1).  (Look at\nthe IPL SOURCE SWITCH in the middle of the Panel.)
+5   source MM1
+1   subtitle Lend CRT $crt to the computer being loaded.  (Look at\nthe BFC CRT switches at Panel's top center.)
+5   crt $crt
+1   subtitle Momentarily flip the spring-loaded IDP $crt toggle.\n(Look at the middle right side of the Panel.)
+5   idpload $idp
+1   subtitle Press the IPL button for GPC $gpc.  (Look at the\nINITIAL PROGRAM LOAD row in Panel mid-left.)\nWatch for red ACTIVITY lamp at Panel bottom.
+5   ipl
+1   subtitle Move GPC $gpc from HALT to STBY to let it run.\n(Look along the bottom left of the Panel.)
+4   mode STANDBY
+1   subtitle The bootstrap loader is now loading the\nsecond-stage loader.  Watch the red\nACTIVITY lamp MM1 at Panel bottom.

# WAIT FOR THE PAGE TO CHANGE HANDS BEFORE BELIEVING WHAT IT SAYS.  A state
# test alone is met by the PREVIOUS computer's menu; see ipl-one-gpc.script.
wait crt $crt new-screen timeout 120
wait crt $crt title GPCIPL timeout 120

+0   subtitle There it is: the GPCIPL MENU, served by GPC $gpc itself.
+4   subtitle Next we ask for Memory Configuration 1 (MC 1) to\nbe loaded.  Use keys ITEM 1 EXEC on keyboard $kb.
+5   keys $kb ITEM 1 EXEC
+1   subtitle Loading ... The GPC is pulling its operating system off the tape.

# loaded: to RUN, and the IPL source back off
wait gpc $gpc mode-tb RUN timeout 120

+0   subtitle Loaded. The MODE talkback for GPC $gpc now reads RUN.\n(Look at the row of indicators just above the\ncaption "MODE", Panel's lower-middle left.)
+5   subtitle Release the BFC CRT.  (Look at\nthe top center of the Panel.)
+2   crt 0
+1   subtitle Flip the computer from STBY mode to RUN mode.\n(Look along the bottom left of the Panel.)
+5   mode RUN
+1   subtitle Turn off the IPL SOURCE.  (Look at\nthe very middle of the Panel.)
+5   source OFF
+1   subtitle Assign the CRT to the proper GPC.
+3   subtitle <left>Use keys GPC/CRT $gpc $crt EXEC
+5   keys GPC/CRT $gpc $crt EXEC
+1   subtitle Success! GPC $gpc is running.
+3   subtitle
